From b7899e62a3a9b1d21838f259adb667d036fc7818 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 21:17:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Show a podcast episode's show notes where lyrics go

An episode's show notes reached the frontend and stopped there: nothing
rendered them. Podcast episodes have no detail view of their own, and the two
places a description could have surfaced both turned them away - the list
subtitle allows only radio and playlists, and the fullscreen player's side panel
was gated to tracks.

Both now let an episode through. In a listing its notes read as the subtitle, the
one line that tells two episodes of the same show apart. In the fullscreen player
the existing panel and its header button now open either a track's lyrics or an
episode's notes, named and iconed for whichever it holds.

The two share the column, not their source: show notes ride along on the queue
item, so there is nothing to fetch and no loading state, and the ~60fps clock
that drives synced lyrics never starts for them. Notes render through
MarkdownText, which sanitises the markup podcast feeds carry and sends its links
to a new tab.
